 <text type="manuscript">
  
  <body>
   <pb xml:id="leaf001r" facs="loc_cm.00041.jpg" type="recto"/>
   <note hand="#h03" place="top" type="authorial">3</note>
  <note rend="circled" type="authorial" place="right" hand="#h02">follow copy punctuation &amp; c</note>
   
    <head><subst><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02" seq="1">Walt Whitman at present.</del><add hand="h03" seq="2" place="below"><metamark function="adjust" target="#j001">&#182;</metamark></add><add hand="#h02" place="below" seq="3" xml:id="j001">About myself at present.</add></subst></head>
     
    <p><subst><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04" seq="1"><del hand="#h03">The poet above named</del></del><add hand="#h04" place="above" seq="2"><subst><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02" seq="3">I</del><add hand="#h02" place="right" rend="marked" seq="4">I</add></subst></add></subst> will soon enter upon <subst hand="#h04"><del rend="overstrike">his</del><add place="above">my</add></subst> 73d year, if <subst rend="overwrite" hand="#h04"><del>he</del><add>I</add></subst> live<del rend="overstrike" hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04">s</del></del>. <subst rend="overwrite"><del>He</del><add>I</add></subst> <subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">has</del><add place="above">have</add></subst> passed an active life, as country school-teacher, printer, carpenter<add hand="#h03">,</add> <subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">and</del><add place="below" seq="2"><metamark function="add" target="#a001">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a001" seq="3">author and</add></subst> journalist, <subst><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02" seq="1">living</del><add place="below" seq="2" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a002">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h03" xml:id="a002" seq="3">domiciled</add></subst> in nearly all the United States and pricipal cities, North and South<subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">.</del><add seq="2">&#8212;</add></subst> <subst rend="overwrite" hand="#h04"><del>He</del><add><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02">I</del></add></subst> went to the front <add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a003">&#8212;</metamark><add place="above" hand="#h03" xml:id="a003"><subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">launching</del><add place="above" seq="2">moving about</add></subst> and occupied</add></add> as army nurse and missionary during the secession war<add hand="#h04">,</add> 1861 to <add hand="#h02">'</add>65, <add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a004">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h03" xml:id="a004">and</add> in the Virginia hospitals and after <add hand="#h03">the</add><add place="below" hand="#h02"><metamark function="add" target="#a005">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h02" place="above" xml:id="a005"><del hand="#h02" rend="overstrike">southern</del></add> battles <add place="below" hand="#h02"><metamark function="add" target="#a006">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h02" place="above" xml:id="a006">of that time,</add> tending the <subst rend="overwrite" hand="#h04"><del>n</del><add>N</add></subst>orthern and <subst hand="#h04"><del>s</del><add>S</add></subst>outhern wounded alike, <add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a007">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h03" xml:id="a007">&#8212;</add> worked <subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">there</del><add place="above" seq="2">down south</add></subst> and in Washington city arduously three years,<add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a008">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h03" xml:id="a008">&#8218;</add> contracted the paralysis which <subst hand="#h04" rend="overwrite"><del>he</del><add><subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">I</del><add place="above" seq="2">I</add></subst></add></subst> <subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike">ha<subst rend="overwrite" hand="#h04"><del>s</del><add>v</add></subst></del><add place="above">have</add></subst> suffered ever since,<add hand="#h02" place="below"><metamark function="add" target="#a009">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h02" xml:id="a009">&#8212;</add> and now live<del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02">s</del> in a little cottage of <subst rend="overwrite" hand="#h04"><del>his</del><add>my</add></subst> <add place="above" hand="#h02">my</add> own, <subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">on</del><add place="above" seq="2">near</add></subst> the Delaware.<add hand="#h03" place="above"><metamark function="add" target="#a010">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h03" xml:id="a010">in New Jersey.</add> <subst><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02" seq="1">His</del><add place="below" hand="#h02" seq="2"><metamark target="#a011" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h02" seq="3" xml:id="a011">My</add></subst> cheif book, unrhymed and unmetrical<add hand="#h02">,</add> <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02" seq="1"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h03" seq="2">"Leaves of Grass"</del></del><add place="below" hand="#h03" seq="3"><metamark function="add" target="#a012">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h03" rend="marked">(it has taken thirty years, peace and was "a borning")</add> has its aim as 
     
     <subst><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04" seq="1">Whitman himself <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h03">says,</del></del><add hand="#h04" place="above" seq="2"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02" seq="3">I have</del><add place="above" hand="#h03" seq="4">once</add><subst rend="overwrite" seq="5"><del>often</del><add place="above" hand="#h03">I</add></subst> <subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike">said</del><add place="above">said</add></subst></add><add hand="#h02">,</add></subst> "to utter the same old human <hi rend="underline">critter</hi> <add place="below" hand="#h02"><metamark function="add" target="#a013">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h02" xml:id="a013">but</add> now in Democratic American modern and scientific conditions". <subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike">Then he has</del><add place="above">Then I have</add></subst> published two prose works "Specimen Days", and a late one </p>
   
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf001v" facs="Loc_jyc.00025_large.jpg" type="verso"/>
   
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf002r" facs="loc_cm.00042.jpg" type="recto"/>
   
   <fw rend="left"><subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">2.</del><add place="top" seq="2">4</add></subst></fw>
   
   <p>"November Boughs". <add hand="#h02" place="below"><metamark function="add" target="#a014">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h02" xml:id="a014">(A little volume "Good Bye my Fancy" is soon to be out.)</add> <subst hand="#h04"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">We do not</del><add place="above" seq="2">I do not</add></subst> propose here to enter the much fought field of <add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a015">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h03" xml:id="a015">any of those</add>the literary criticism of <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h03">these</del> works.<add hand="#h02">;</add> On another page however are presented some <subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">late</del><add seq="2" place="above">fresh</add></subst> poetic pieces of <subst hand="#h04"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">Whitman.</del><add place="above" seq="2">mine.</add></subst> The portrait in this number was taken last summer and is a pretty good likeness)</p>
   
   <p xml:id="d001"><add hand="#h02" place="above" rend="marked" xml:id="j002"><add hand="#h03"><metamark function="adjust" target="#j002">&#182;</metamark></add> Now for <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">some</del><add place="above" seq="2">a few</add></subst> portraiture <add hand="#h03">or descriptive</add> bits.</add> To-day in the upper <add place="below" hand="#h04"><metamark function="add" target="#a016">&#8248;</metamark></add><del hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h03"><add place="above" hand="#h04"><unclear reason="illegible" cert="high" resp="#cm">part</unclear></add></del></del> of a little wooden house of two stories near the Delaware river, east shore, sixty miles up from the sea, is a rather large 20 by 20 low ceiling<subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">e</del><add place="above" seq="2"><metamark function="emphasize" target="#e001">&#711;</metamark></add><add place="above" seq="3" xml:id="e001">'</add></subst>d room something like a big old ships cabin.</p>
   
   <addSpan rend="marked" hand="#h02" spanTo="#a017"/><metamark function="delete" target="#d001 #d002"/><anchor xml:id="a017"/>
   
   <p xml:id="d002">The floor, three quaters of it with an ingrain carpet, is half covered by a deep litter of books, papers<add hand="#h02">,</add> magazines, thrown down letters and circulars, rejected manuscripts, memoranda, bits of light or strong twine<add hand="#h02">,</add> a bundle to be "expressed", and two or three venerable scrap books. In the room <subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">are</del><add seq="2" place="above">stand</add></subst> two large tables (one of ancient solid mahogany with immense leaves) covered by a jumble of <add place="below" hand="#h02"><metamark function="add" target="#a018">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h02" xml:id="a018">more</add> papers, a varied and</p>
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf002v" facs="loc_jyc.00027_large.jpg" type="verso"/>
   
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf003r" facs="loc_cm.00043.jpg" type="recto"/>
   
   <fw rend="left"><subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">3.</del><add place="top" seq="2">5</add></subst></fw>
   
   <p xml:id="d004">copious array of writing materials, <subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">some</del><add seq="2" place="above">several</add></subst> glass and china vessels or jars, some <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02">little ones</del> with cologne-water, others with real honey, granulated sugar, a large bunch of beautiful yellow chru<subst hand="#h02" rend="overwrite"><del>s</del><add>y</add></subst>anthemums, some letters and enveloped papers ready for the post office, many photographs<add hand="#h02">,</add> and a hundred indescribable things besides. There are all around many books, some quite handsome editions, some half covered by dust<add hand="#h04">,</add> some within reach, evidently used, ( good sized print<add hand="#h02">,</add> no type less than long primer) <add hand="#h03" place="below"><metamark function="add" target="#a019">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h03" xml:id="a019">some maps,</add> the Bible, ( the strong cheap edition of the English crown) Homer, Shakspere, Walter Scott, Emerson<add hand="#h02">,</add> Ticknor's "Spanish Literature", John Caryle's Dante, Felton's Greece, <add place="below" hand="#h02"><metamark function="add" target="#a020">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h02">George Sand's Consuelo,</add> a very choice little Epicteteus, <add place="below" hand="#h02"><metamark function="add" target="#a021">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h02" place="above" xml:id="a021">some novel,</add> the latest foreign and American monthlies, quaterlies<add hand="#h02">,</add> and so on. There being quite a strew of <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02">slips and printer's</del> proofs <add place="below" hand="#h02"><metamark function="add" target="#a022">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h02" xml:id="a022">and slips,</add> the place with its quaint old fashioned calmness has also a smack of something alert and of current work</p> 
   
   <metamark function="delete" target="#d003 #d004"><add hand="#h02" rend="marked">run in next</add></metamark>
   
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf003v" facs="loc_jyc.00029_large.jpg" type="verso"/>
   
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf004r" facs="loc_cm.00044.jpg" type="recto"/>
   
   <fw rend="left"><subst hand="#h03"><del seq="1" rend="overstrike">4.</del><add place="top" seq="2">6</add></subst></fw>
   
   <metamark function="delete" target="#d003 #d004"><add hand="#h02" rend="marked" place="above">run in</add></metamark>
   
   <p xml:id="d003">There are several trunks and depositaries backed up at the wall<add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a023">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h03" xml:id="a023">s</add>; <add hand="#h03">(</add>one well-bound and big b<subst rend="overwrite"><del>x</del><add>o</add></subst><add hand="#h04">x</add><add hand="#h04" xml:id="a024"><choice><orig><metamark function="add" target="#a024">|</metamark></orig><reg> </reg></choice></add><add hand="#h02" place="above">box</add>came by express lately from Washington city, after storage there for nearly twenty years.<add hand="#h03">)</add> Indeed the whole room is a sort of a result and storage collection of <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h03"><restore xml:id="r001" rend="dotted"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04">its owners</del></restore></del><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02"><add place="above">my</add></del><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h03"><add hand="#h02" place="left" rend="circled"><metamark function="restore" target="#r001">stet</metamark></add></del><add hand="#h03" place="below"><metamark function="add" target="#a025">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h03" xml:id="a025">my own</add> past life. <subst><del hand="#h03" rend="overstrike" seq="4"><del hand="#h02" rend="overstrike" seq="2"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04" seq="1">He has</del> <subst hand="#h04"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1"><subst rend="overwrite" hand="#h04"><del>t</del><add>T</add></subst>he</del><add place="above" seq="2">I have here</add></subst></del></del><add place="below" seq="3"><metamark function="add" target="#a026">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a026" seq="3">I have here</add></subst> various editions of <subst hand="#h04"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">his</del><add place="above" seq="2">my</add></subst> own writings, and sells them upon request; one is a big volume, <subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1"><subst hand="#h04"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">his</del><add place="above" seq="2">my</add></subst></del><add place="below" seq="2"><metamark function="add" target="#a027">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" seq="2" xml:id="a027">of</add><add hand="#h03" seq="3">my</add></subst> complete poems and prose, <add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a028">&#8248;</metamark><add place="above" hand="#h03">1000 pages,</add></add> autobiography<add hand="#h02">,</add> essays, speeches, portraits from life etc. Another is a little <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02">"</del><hi rend="underline">Leaves of Grass</hi><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02">"</del>, latest date, morocco bound, in pocket book form.</p>
   
   <metamark function="adjust" target="#j003"><add hand="#h03">&#182;</add></metamark><p xml:id="j003">Fortunately<add hand="#h02">,</add> the apartment is quite roomy. There are three windows in <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02">the</del> front. At one side is the stove<add hand="#h03">,</add> with a cheerful fire of oak wood, near by a good supply of fresh sticks, whose faint aroma is plain. On another side is the bed with snow white coverled and woolen blakents. <add hand="#h04"><metamark function="emphasize" target="#d005">&#11812;</metamark></add><del hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04" xml:id="d005">As I have often been in his room</del> <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04" xml:id="d006"><subst rend="overwrite" hand="#h04"><del>t</del><add>T</add></subst>he whole description i<subst rend="overwrite" hand="#h04"><del>d</del><add>s</add></subst> from life.</del></del><add hand="#h04"><metamark function="emphasize" target="#d006">|</metamark></add> Towards the windows <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02">of the place</del> is a huge arm-chair, ( a Christmas present </p>

   <pb xml:id="leaf004v" facs="loc_jyc.00031_large.jpg" type="verso"/>
   
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf005r" facs="loc_cm.00045.jpg" type="recto"/>
   
   <fw rend="left"><subst hand="#h03"><del seq="1" rend="overstrike">5.</del><add place="top" seq="2">7</add></subst></fw>
   
   <p>from Thomas Donaldson's young daughter and son, Philadelphia) timbered as <subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">from</del><add seq="2" place="above">by</add></subst> stout ship<add hand="#h04">'</add>s spars, yellow polished, ample<add hand="#h03">,</add> with <subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">satin</del><add seq="2" place="above">ratan</add></subst> woven seat and back<add hand="#h04">,</add> and over the latter a great wide wol<subst hand="#h02" rend="overwrite"><del>o</del><add>f</add></subst>skin of hairy black and silver<add hand="#h02">,</add> spread to guard against cold and draught. <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h03">Strength<add hand="#h02">,</add> plainness, ease and comfort with what may be called</del> <subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h03" seq="1"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h03" seq="1">a</del></del><add place="above" seq="2" rend="tripleUnderline">A</add></subst> time-worn look and scent of old oak<add hand="#h02">,</add> <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02">woods</del> attach to both the chair and the person occupying it. <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04">This is Walt Whitman the poet.</del></del>
   <note type="editorial" hand="#h04" rend="marked" place="inline"><gap reason="illegible" extent="one word"/> off</note></p>
   
   <p xml:id="j004"><add place="above" hand="#h03"><metamark function="adjust" target="#j004">&#182;</metamark></add><add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark function="add" target="#a029">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h03" xml:id="a029">But</add>Propbably <subst hand="#h04" rend="overwrite"><del>we</del><add>I</add></subst> can give no more authentic brief sketch <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h03">of</del> <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h03"><subst hand="#h04"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">W.W.</del><add place="above" seq="2">myself</add></subst></del> than <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02">the one we got</del> "from an old remembrance copy", <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04">he</del> <subst hand="#h04"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">has</del></del><add place="above" seq="2">where I</add></subst> <subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">lately</del><add place="below" seq="2"><metamark function="add" target="#a030">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" seq="2" xml:id="a030">have lately</add></subst> put <add hand="#h02" place="below"><metamark function="add" target="#a031">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h02" xml:id="a031">myself</add> on record <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h03"><del hand="#h02" rend="overstrike"><subst hand="#h04"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">himself</del><add place="above" seq="2">myself</add></subst></del></del> as follows:</p>
   
   <p>Was born May 31, 1819, in my father's farm-house, at West Hills, L.T., New York State. My parents<add hand="#h02">'</add> folks mostly farmers and sailors- on my father<add hand="#h02">'</add>s side, of English- on my mother<add hand="#h02">'</add>s (Van Velsor's) from Hollandic immigration. There was<add hand="#h02">,</add> first and last, a large family of children;( I was the second)</p>
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf005v" facs="loc_jyc.00033_large.jpg" type="verso"/>
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf006r" facs="loc_cm.00046.jpg" type="recto"/>
   
   <fw rend="left"><subst hand="#h03"><del seq="1" rend="overstrike">6.</del><add place="top" seq="2">8</add></subst></fw>
   
   <p>We moved to brooklyn while I was still a little one in frpcks- and there in B. I grew up out of frocks&#8211; then as a child and boy went to the public schools&#8211; then to work in a printing office.</p>
   
   <p>When only sixteen o<subst hand="#h04"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">t</del><add place="above" seq="2">r</add></subst> seventeen years old, and for <subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">two</del><add place="above" seq="2">three</add></subst> years afterward<del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04">s</del>, I went to teaching schools down in queens and Suffolk counties, Long Island, and "boarded round" Then,returning to Ney York, worked as a printer and writer, (with an occasional shy at "poetry".)</p>
   
   <p xml:id="j005"><add hand="#h03"><metamark function="adjust" target="#j005">&#182;</metamark></add>1848<subst rend="overwrite"><del>)</del><add>&#8211;</add></subst>'9-- About this <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02"><add place="below" hand="#h02"><metamark function="add" target="#a032">&#8248;</metamark></add></del> time <add place="below" hand="#h02"><metamark function="add" target="#a032">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h02" rend="marked" xml:id="a032">&#8212;after <subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike"  seq="1">lots</del><add place="below" seq="2"><metamark function="add" target="#a033">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" seq="2" xml:id="a033">eight or nine years,</add></subst> of experiences, and fun and work in New York and Brooklyn &#8212;</add> went off on a leisurely journey and working exp<subst rend="overwrite"><del><gap reason="cancelled" extent="a few letters"/></del><add>ped</add></subst>ition( my brother Jeff with me) through all the Middle States, and down the Ohio and Mississippi rivers. Lived a while in New Orleans, and worked there. (Have lived quite a good deal in the Southern States.) After a time, plodded back northward, up the Mississippi, the Missouri <subst><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02">etc.</del><add hand="#h04" place="above">etc.</add></subst>, and around to, and by the way of, the great lakes, Michigan, Huron and Erie,
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf006v" facs="loc_jyc.00035_large.jpg" type="verso"/>
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf007r" facs="loc_cm.00047.jpg" type="recto"/>
   
   <fw rend="left"><subst hand="#h03"><del seq="1" rend="overstrike">7.</del><add place="top" seq="2">9</add></subst></fw>
   
to Niagra Falls and lower Canada&#8211; finally returning through Central New York, and down the Hudson.</p>
   
   <!-- <metamark function="delete" target="#j005 #j006"><add hand="#h03" rend="marked" place="right">run in</add></metamark>-->
   
   <p xml:id="j006" rend="marked"><subst hand="#h03"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h03"><add place="left" hand="#h03"><metamark function="adjust" target="#j006">&#182;</metamark></add></del><add place="above" rend="marked"><metamark function="delete" target="#j006 #j005">run in</metamark></add></subst>1851&#8211;'54<add hand="#h02">&#8211;</add> occupied in house&#8211;building in Brooklyn. (For a little while of the first part of that time in printing a daily and weekly paper.)</p>
   
   <metamark function="adjust" target="#j007"><add hand="#h03">&#8211;</add></metamark><p xml:id="j007">1855.<add hand="#h02">&#8211;</add> Lost my dear father this year by death.. Commenced putting <hi rend="underline">Leaves of Grass</hi> <space dim="horizontal" extent="about five characters"></space> to press, for good&#8211; after many MS. doings and undoings&#8211; (I had great trouble in leaving out the stock<del hand="#h03">"</del> <add hand="#h03">"</add>poetical" touches&#8211; but succeeded at last.<add hand="#h02" rend="marked">)</add></p>
   
   <p>The book has since had some eight hitches or stages of growth, with one annex, <add hand="#h02">(</add>and another to come out in 1891<add hand="#h02">,</add> which will complete it.<add hand="#h02">)</add></p>
   
   <metamark function="adjust" target="#j008"><add hand="#h03">&#182;</add></metamark><p xml:id="j008">1862.&#8211; In December of this year went down to the field of War in Virginia. My brother George reported badly wounded in the Fredericksburgh fight. ( For 1865 and'64 see <hi rend="underline">Specimen Days</hi>)</p>
   
   <p xml:id="j009" rend="marked"><subst hand="#h02"><del><add hand="#h03"><metamark function="adjust" target="#j009">&#182;</metamark></add></del><add place="above" rend="marked"><metamark function="delete" target="#j009 #j008">run in</metamark></add></subst>
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf007v" facs="loc_jyc.00037_large.jpg" type="verso"/>
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf008r" facs="loc_cm.00048.jpg" type="recto"/>
   
   <fw rend="left"><subst hand="#h03"><del seq="1" rend="overstrike">8.</del><add place="top" seq="2">10</add></subst></fw>
   
  the Attorney General's Office, Washington.</p>
   
   <p>(New York and Brooklyn seem more like <hi rend="underline">home</hi>, as I was born near, and brought up in them, and lived, man and boy, for 30 years. But I lived some years in Washington, and have visited, and partially lived, in most of the Western and eastern cities)</p>
   
   <p></p>
